{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_bdrk_01TqV8PcEhVsUqeZYe496uA8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01VeQwJMsKzKZJgaQp28C4Pq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"source /home/cyanz/miniconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh && conda activate wave && python3 << 'PYEOF'\nimport sympy as sp\nimport numpy as np\nimport sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '/local/home/cyanz/wave_PINN')\nfrom verify_engine import x, t, c, x0, alpha, s, lam, build_operators, run_verification\n\n# STRATEGY: Use the double-log ansatz but with s depending on c AND x-bounded.\n# Actually wait - let me try something genuinely new.\n# \n# All rounds 2-5 used log-based ansatze with alpha=1.\n# The key structural issue: with alpha=1, tilde_sq(psi) = sq_psi for the double-log.\n# \n# What if we try a different alpha? With alpha != 1, the L operator has a different structure.\n# For the double-log: L = lam*(lam - alpha + 1)*phi*sq_psi\n# Condition 1 requires L1 <= L <= -L1, which is |L| <= -L1 (since L1 <= 0).\n# \n# Actually, let me try a completely different approach:\n# ψ = -log(1+t) - log(1+x), alpha=2, lam=-1/20\n# With alpha=2: (alpha-1) = 1, so:\n# L = lam^2*phi*tilde - lam*phi*sq = lam*phi*(lam*tilde - sq)\n# For double-log: tilde = sq, so L = lam*phi*(lam-1)*sq = lam*(lam-1)*phi*sq\n# = (-1/20)*(-1/20-1)*phi*sq = (-1/20)*(-21/20)*phi*sq = 21/(400)*phi*sq\n# \n# L1 = lam^2*phi*grad^2 + lam*phi*lap\n# For double-log: grad^2 = (ψ_t^2 + c^2*ψ_x^2) = P, lap = (ψ_tt + c^2*ψ_xx) = P (same!)\n# So L1 = lam*(lam+1)*phi*P = (-1/20)(19/20)*phi*P = -19/400*phi*P\n# Since P > 0 and phi > 0: L1 < 0. ✓\n#\n# Condition 1: |L| <= -L1\n# |L| = 21/400*phi*|sq| (sq can be positive or negative depending on x,t)\n# -L1 = 19/400*phi*P\n# Need: 21/400*|sq| <= 19/400*P, i.e., 21*|sq| <= 19*P\n# sq = 1/(1+t)^2 - c^2/(1+x)^2\n# P = 1/(1+t)^2 + c^2/(1+x)^2\n# |sq| <= P always (since |a-b| <= |a|+|b| = a+b when a,b >= 0)\n# So 21*|sq| <= 21*P. We need 21*P <= 19*P which is 21 <= 19. FALSE!\n#\n# So alpha=2 breaks condition 1 for the double-log. The issue: |L|/phi > |L1|/phi.\n# With alpha=1: L = lam*(lam-0)*phi*sq = lam^2*phi*sq, |L|/phi = lam^2*|sq| = |sq|/400\n# -L1/phi = -lam*(lam+1)*P = 19P/400\n# Need: |sq|/400 <= 19P/400, i.e., |sq| <= 19*P. Always true since |sq| <= P <= 19P. ✓\n# \n# With alpha=a: L = lam*(lam-a+1)*phi*sq, |L|/phi = |lam*(lam-a+1)|*|sq|\n# -L1/phi = -lam*(lam+1)*P = |lam|*|lam+1|*P\n# Need: |lam*(lam-a+1)|*|sq| <= |lam|*|lam+1|*P\n# i.e., |lam-a+1|*|sq| <= |lam+1|*P\n# Since |sq| <= P: sufficient to have |lam-a+1| <= |lam+1|\n# With lam = -1/N: lam-a+1 = -1/N - a + 1 = (N-1-Na)/N = (1-a) - 1/N\n# lam+1 = 1-1/N = (N-1)/N\n# |lam-a+1| <= |lam+1| iff |1-a-1/N| <= (N-1)/N\n# For a=1: |−1/N| = 1/N ≤ (N−1)/N. ✓ (this is what rounds 2-5 used)\n# For a<1: 1-a-1/N. If a < 1-1/N, this is positive = 1-a-1/N. Need 1-a-1/N <= (N-1)/N\n#   => 1-a <= 1 => a >= 0. ✓ for any a >= 0.\n# For a>1: lam-a+1 = 1-a-1/N < 0. |1-a-1/N| = a-1+1/N. Need a-1+1/N <= (N-1)/N\n#   => a <= 1-2/N. But a > 1, so this FAILS for a > 1.\n# So alpha must be in [0, 1] for condition 1 to hold (with the double-log and lam=-1/N).\n# Actually alpha in [0, 1-2/N+1] = [0, 1] roughly.\n#\n# With alpha < 1, the L2 O(s) coefficient changes.\n# O(s) term in L2: (1/2)*|s| * ((alpha-1)*lam - lam^2) * sq(phi*tilde)\n# Wait, I need to be more careful. With alpha=1, (alpha-1) = 0, so the first part of L2 \n# only has the -s*lam^2*sq(phi*tilde)/2 term. With alpha != 1:\n# L2_O(s) = (1/2)*( (alpha-1)*s*lam*sq(phi*sq_psi) - s*lam^2*sq(phi*tilde_sq) )\n# For double-log: sq_psi = tilde_sq, so:\n# = (1/2)*s*lam * ( (alpha-1)*sq(phi*tilde) - lam*sq(phi*tilde) )\n# = (1/2)*s*lam*(alpha-1-lam)*sq(phi*tilde)\n# With s<0, lam<0: s*lam = |s|*|lam| > 0\n# (alpha-1-lam) = alpha-1+|lam|\n# For alpha in [0,1]: alpha-1+|lam| = (alpha-1) + 1/N\n# For alpha=1: = 1/N > 0\n# For alpha=0: = -1 + 1/N < 0 (for N>1). SIGN FLIP!\n# For alpha = 1-1/N = (N-1)/N: = -1/N + 1/N = 0. The O(s) term VANISHES!\n#\n# Hmm. If the O(s) term vanishes, L2 is purely O(s^3), which is bad.\n# For alpha close to 1, the O(s) term is positive and strongest.\n# So alpha=1 maximizes the O(s) positive contribution.\n#\n# Let me try a completely different approach. Instead of the double-log, \n# what about a function where L2 is manifestly non-negative?\n#\n# The L2 expression is very complex. Let me try to find a ψ where many L2 terms vanish.\n# If tilde_sq(ψ) = 0 (eikonal equation): |ψ_t| = c|ψ_x|\n# Then ALL the s^3 terms vanish (they all contain tilde_sq(ψ)).\n# And L2_O(s) = (1/2)*((alpha-1)*s*lam*sq(phi*sq_psi) - s*lam^2*sq(phi*0))\n# = (1/2)*(alpha-1)*s*lam*sq(phi*sq_psi)\n# For alpha=1: this is 0, so L2 = 0. Not helpful (need L2 > 0).\n# For alpha != 1: L2 = (1/2)*(alpha-1)*s*lam*sq(phi*sq_psi)\n# With s<0, lam<0: s*lam > 0.\n# Need (alpha-1)*sq(phi*sq_psi) > 0.\n# If sq_psi > 0 and sq(phi*sq_psi) > 0: need alpha > 1. But alpha > 1 may break Cond 1.\n#\n# Eikonal ψ with ψ_t = c*ψ_x (forward characteristic):\n# ψ = f(x + ct) for any f.\n# Then ψ_t = c*f', ψ_x = f', ψ_tt = c^2*f'', ψ_xx = f''\n# sq_psi = c^2*f'' - c^2*f'' = 0\n# tilde_sq(psi) = c^2*(f')^2 - c^2*(f')^2 = 0 ✓\n# BUT sq_psi = 0 too! So ALL terms in L2 vanish (through sq_psi and tilde factors).\n# L2 = 0 identically. Not useful.\n#\n# What about ψ_t = -c*ψ_x (backward characteristic)?\n# ψ = g(x - ct)\n# ψ_t = -c*g', ψ_x = g', tilde_sq = c^2(g')^2 - c^2(g')^2 = 0\n# Same issue. L2 = 0.\n#\n# What about MIXED: ψ = f(x+ct) + g(x-ct)?\n# tilde_sq = (c*f'-c*g')^2 - c^2*(f'+g')^2 = c^2((f'-g')^2 - (f'+g')^2) = -4c^2*f'*g'\n# sq_psi = c^2*(f''+g'') - c^2*(f''+g'') = 0  (still zero!)\n# So sq_psi = 0, tilde_sq = -4c^2*f'*g'\n# L = lam^2*phi*tilde - 0 = lam^2*phi*(-4c^2*f'*g')\n# L1 = lam^2*phi*(tilde_sq_grad) + lam*phi*(lap)\n# where tilde_sq_grad = ψ_t^2 + c^2*ψ_x^2 = c^2(f'-g')^2 + c^2(f'+g')^2 = 2c^2(f'^2+g'^2)\n# and lap = ψ_tt + c^2*ψ_xx = c^2(f''+g'') + c^2(f''+g'') = 2c^2(f''+g'')\n# For L1 <= 0: lam^2*2c^2(f'^2+g'^2) + lam*2c^2(f''+g'') <= 0\n# Need: lam*(lam(f'^2+g'^2) + (f''+g'')) <= 0 [since 2c^2 > 0]\n# With lam < 0: need lam(f'^2+g'^2) + (f''+g'') >= 0\n# i.e., f''+g'' >= |lam|(f'^2+g'^2)\n#\n# This is very promising! If f and g are chosen carefully (e.g., concave-down: f'', g'' < 0),\n# the inequality f''+g'' >= |lam|*(f'^2+g'^2) requires f''+g'' negative enough.\n# But then f''+g'' < 0, so need |lam|(f'^2+g'^2) <= f''+g'' < 0. Contradiction.\n# Wait: with lam < 0, the condition is lam(f'^2+g'^2) + (f''+g'') >= 0.\n# lam < 0, so lam*(f'^2+g'^2) < 0. Need (f''+g'') >= -lam*(f'^2+g'^2) = |lam|*(f'^2+g'^2) > 0.\n# So we need f''+g'' > 0. Both f and g must have POSITIVE second derivatives (convex).\n#\n# If f(u) = -log(1+u) for u = x+ct: f' = -1/(1+u), f'' = 1/(1+u)^2 > 0 ✓\n# If g(v) = -log(1+v) for v = x-ct: g' = -1/(1+v), g'' = 1/(1+v)^2 > 0 ✓\n# But v = x - ct: for t > x/c, v < 0, so 1+v could be negative!\n# Domain: x >= 0, t in [0,T]. So v = x-ct >= -cT. For 1+v > 0: need x-ct > -1, i.e., x > ct-1.\n# At x=0, t=T: v = -cT, 1+v = 1-cT. For cT > 1, this is negative. log(1+v) undefined!\n# So g(x-ct) = -log(1+x-ct) doesn't work for large t.\n#\n# Fix: use g(v) = -log(1+x+ct) instead? But that's not a function of (x-ct).\n# Or use g(v) = -log(K + x - ct) with K large enough.\n# For K > cT: 1+K+x-ct = 1+K+v > 1+K-cT > 0. ✓\n# But K depends on c and T... this is getting messy.\n#\n# ANOTHER IDEA: ψ = -log(1+x+ct) - log(1+x-ct+M) where M = M(c,T) > cT.\n# This is a function of two characteristic variables. Let me explore this.\n\nprint(\"Exploring characteristic-based ansatz...\")\nprint(\"ψ = -log(1+x+ct) - log(M+x-ct) with M > cT\")\nprint()\n\n# Let u = x + ct, v = x - ct\n# ψ = -log(1+u) - log(M+v) where M > cT ensures M+v = M+x-ct > 0 on the domain.\n# ψ_t = -c/(1+u) + c/(M+v) = c*(-1/(1+u) + 1/(M+v))\n# ψ_x = -1/(1+u) - 1/(M+v)\n# ψ_tt = c^2/(1+u)^2 + c^2/(M+v)^2  [both positive]\n# ψ_xx = 1/(1+u)^2 + 1/(M+v)^2      [both positive]\n# sq_psi = ψ_tt - c^2*ψ_xx = c^2/(1+u)^2 + c^2/(M+v)^2 - c^2/(1+u)^2 - c^2/(M+v)^2 = 0!\n# tilde_sq = ψ_t^2 - c^2*ψ_x^2 = c^2(-1/(1+u)+1/(M+v))^2 - c^2(1/(1+u)+1/(M+v))^2\n#          = c^2*[(-1/(1+u)+1/(M+v))^2 - (1/(1+u)+1/(M+v))^2]\n#          = c^2*(-4/((1+u)(M+v)))  [using (a-b)^2-(a+b)^2 = -4ab with a=1/(1+u), b=1/(M+v)]\n#          = -4c^2/((1+u)(M+v))\n\nprint(\"sq_psi = 0 (because ψ = f(x+ct) + g(x-ct))\")\nprint(\"tilde_sq(ψ) = -4c²/((1+x+ct)(M+x-ct))\")\nprint()\n\n# With sq_psi = 0 and alpha=1:\n# L = lam^2*phi*tilde_sq - 0 = lam^2*phi*tilde_sq\n# Since tilde_sq < 0: L < 0 (with lam^2 > 0, phi > 0).\n# L1 = lam^2*phi*(ψ_t^2 + c^2*ψ_x^2) + lam*phi*(ψ_tt + c^2*ψ_xx)\n# ψ_t^2 + c^2*ψ_x^2 = c^2*(1/(1+u)^2 - 2/((1+u)(M+v)) + 1/(M+v)^2) + c^2*(1/(1+u)^2 + 2/((1+u)(M+v)) + 1/(M+v)^2)\n# = 2c^2*(1/(1+u)^2 + 1/(M+v)^2)  [the cross terms cancel]\n# ψ_tt + c^2*ψ_xx = c^2*(1/(1+u)^2 + 1/(M+v)^2) + c^2*(1/(1+u)^2 + 1/(M+v)^2)\n# = 2c^2*(1/(1+u)^2 + 1/(M+v)^2)\n#\n# So grad^2 = lap for this ansatz too! (Same self-similar property as double-log)\n# L1 = lam*(lam+1)*phi*(grad^2) = lam*(lam+1)*phi*2c^2*(1/(1+u)^2 + 1/(M+v)^2)\n# With lam = -1/N: lam*(lam+1) = (-1/N)(1-1/N) = -(N-1)/N^2 < 0. So L1 < 0. ✓\n#\n# Condition 1: |L| <= -L1\n# |L| = lam^2*phi*|tilde_sq| = (1/N^2)*phi*4c^2/((1+u)(M+v))\n# -L1 = (N-1)/N^2 * phi * 2c^2*(1/(1+u)^2 + 1/(M+v)^2)\n# Need: 4c^2/((1+u)(M+v)) <= (N-1)*2c^2*(1/(1+u)^2 + 1/(M+v)^2)\n# i.e., 2/((1+u)(M+v)) <= (N-1)*(1/(1+u)^2 + 1/(M+v)^2)\n# By AM-GM: 1/(1+u)^2 + 1/(M+v)^2 >= 2/((1+u)(M+v))\n# So RHS >= 2(N-1)/((1+u)(M+v)) >= 2/(1+u)(M+v) when N >= 2.\n# And we need 2/((1+u)(M+v)) <= 2(N-1)/((1+u)(M+v)), i.e., 1 <= N-1, i.e., N >= 2.\n# With N = 20: N-1 = 19 >= 2. ✓\n\nprint(\"Condition 1: Holds for N >= 2 (i.e., lam = -1/N with N >= 2)\")\nprint()\n\n# Condition 2: lam*ψ -> +∞ as x -> +∞\n# lam*ψ = -lam*(log(1+x+ct) + log(M+x-ct)) = |lam|*(log(1+x+ct) + log(M+x-ct))\n# As x -> +∞: both logs -> +∞. So lam*ψ -> +∞. ✓\n\nprint(\"Condition 2: ✓ (logarithmic growth)\")\nprint()\n\n# Sufficient condition: (L1)^2 - (L)^2 >= c^2*(phi_xt)^2\n# L1 = -(N-1)/N^2 * phi * P where P = 2c^2*(A^2 + B^2), A = 1/(1+u), B = 1/(M+v)\n# L = phi/N^2 * tilde_sq = -4c^2*phi/(N^2*(1+u)(M+v))\n# L^2 = 16c^4*phi^2/(N^4*(1+u)^2*(M+v)^2)\n# L1^2 = (N-1)^2/N^4 * phi^2 * 4c^4*(A^2+B^2)^2\n# L1^2 - L^2 = phi^2*c^4/N^4 * [4(N-1)^2*(A^2+B^2)^2 - 16*A^2*B^2]\n# = phi^2*c^4/N^4 * 4 * [(N-1)^2*(A^2+B^2)^2 - 4*A^2*B^2]\n# By AM-GM: (A^2+B^2)^2 >= 4A^2*B^2, so:\n# (N-1)^2*(A^2+B^2)^2 >= (N-1)^2*4*A^2*B^2 >= 4A^2B^2 when (N-1)^2 >= 1, i.e., N >= 2.\n# So L1^2 - L^2 >= 0. ✓\n# \n# Now need to check L1^2 - L^2 >= c^2*(phi_xt)^2.\n# phi = exp(lam*ψ) = ((1+u)(M+v))^{1/N}\n# phi_x = phi*lam*ψ_x = phi*(-1/N)*(-1/(1+u) - 1/(M+v))\n# phi_t = phi*lam*ψ_t = phi*(-1/N)*c*(-1/(1+u) + 1/(M+v))\n# phi_xt = d_x(phi_t)\n# This gets complex. Let me compute it symbolically.\n\nM = sp.Symbol('M', positive=True)\nu_var = x + c*t\nv_var = x - c*t\npsi_char = -sp.ln(1 + u_var) - sp.ln(M + v_var)\n\n# Check with a concrete M\n# M = c*T + 1 ensures M + v = 1 + x - ct + cT > 0 for t in [0,T], x >= 0\n# But T is not a symbol in the engine. Let's try M = 2*c + 1 (works for T <= 2 at least)\n# Actually, since the problem is for arbitrary T, we need M to depend on T.\n# But T might not be a symbol. Let me check if we can just use a large M.\n\n# For now, let's try a specific case and see if L2 > 0.\nprint(\"Testing characteristic ansatz with M = 2*c (ensures positivity for T <= 2)...\")\n\npsi_test = -sp.ln(1 + x + c*t) - sp.ln(2*c + x - c*t)\nsubs_test = {alpha: 1, lam: sp.Rational(-1, 20), s: sp.Rational(-1, 10)}\n\nops = build_operators(psi_test, subs_test)\nL2_val = ops['L2']\nL2_simplified = sp.simplify(L2_val)\nprint(\"L2 computed, checking numerically...\")\n\n# Numerical check\nf = sp.lambdify((x, t, c), L2_simplified, 'numpy')\nx_arr = np.concatenate([np.linspace(0, 100, 30), np.logspace(2, 20, 30)])\nt_arr = np.linspace(0, 1.9, 20)  # t < 2 for M=2c safety\nc_vals = [0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 5.0]\n\nglobal_min = float('inf')\nfor c_val in c_vals:\n    X, T = np.meshgrid(x_arr, t_arr)\n    try:\n        Z = f(X, T, c_val)\n        mask = np.isfinite(Z) & (2*c_val + X - c_val*T > 0.01)  # ensure M+v > 0\n        if np.any(mask):\n            local_min = float(np.min(Z[mask]))\n            global_min = min(global_min, local_min)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"  c={c_val}: error {e}\")\n\nprint(f\"Global min L2 = {global_min:.6e}\")\n\nPYEOF\n","description":"Test characteristic-based ansatz","timeout":300000}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7354,"cache_read_input_tokens":137547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7354,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"760dc304-8a9b-499d-91d9-5ac15b9d654b","uuid":"d3498f25-3d93-42b0-bc92-965aa1443595"}
